    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/on-campus-jobs/": {
      "title": "On-Campus and Local Jobs",
      "description": "On-Campus and Local Jobs | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services On-Campus Jobs Students: On-Campus Jobs (Handshake) Students: Local Jobs (Handshake) Departments: Hiring Huskies On-Campus and Local Jobs A part-time job is a great opportunity to develop transferable skills, find mentorship,\n                           stretch into problem-solving and teamwork situations, and make connections across\n                           campus. In addition to earning money, students who work on campus gain experiences\n                           for their resume and stories to tell in interviews, even if the job is not in the\n                           same technical field the student is studying for. There are many opportunities available throughout the year, both on campus and in\n                           the community. Most on-campus jobs are open to all students, but there are some restrictions\n                           for federal work-study and for international students. Work-Study FAQ Work-study is a form of federal financial aid. Positions marked as work-study on Handshake\n                                    and on the list below are reserved for those who have work-study as a part of their\n                                    financial aid package. Students with work-study jobs will receive regular pay, which\n                                    they can use toward their expenses. For more information on work-study and eligibility,\n                                    visit the Student Financial Services Center site , email workstudy@mtu.edu , or call 906-487-2622. International Students F-1 J-1 International students may work on campus, paid by Michigan Tech, up to 20 hours per week during the fall and spring semesters and up to 40 hours per week during the summer. International students who want to work in their field to gain experience must participate\n                                    in a training program: Curricular Practical Training or Optional Practical Training for F-1 students and Academic Training for J-1 students. Job Postings On-campus Jobs on Handshake Handshake Local Jobs on Handshake Handshake Orientation, Success Coach, and Peer Mentor Jobs for 2025-26 WWCSS Hiring Site More Local (off-campus) Jobs PMTC Departments That Frequently Post On-campus Jobs Department Where to find job postings How to apply Athletics website Center for Educational Outreach Handshake and word of mouth special application Center for Technology and Training word of mouth College of Business Handshake Handshake College of Computing Handshake Handshake College of Forest Resources and Environmental Science website Department of Chemical Engineering Handshake Handshake Department of Psychology and Human Factors Handshake Handshake Department of Social Sciences word of mouth Facilities Handshake Handshake Graduate School Handshake Handshake Human Resources word of mouth Husky Eats website International Programs and Services Handshake and emails resume and cover letter Math Learning Center website application McNair Scholars word of mouth Merchandising Operations Handshake resume and cover letter Office of Sustainability and Resilience Handshake application Student Affairs , Dean of Students , and Waino Wahtera Center for Student Success Handshake WWCSS Hiring Site Handshake special application Student Financial Services Handshake Handshake Transportation Services Handshake Handshake Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/fair/": {
      "title": "Career Fair",
      "description": "Career Fair | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Career Fair Fall 2026 Career Fair Tuesday, September 29 Noon–5 p.m. Student Development Complex Career Fair Michigan Tech's semi-annual Career Fair is open to all Michigan Tech students (current and past) of all majors, and it's the\n                           best opportunity for employers of all industries to meet and hire the best and brightest.\n                           Our Career Fair is one of the largest in the country. We bring more than 400 companies\n                           and 2,000 recruiters to meet over 4,000 students—more than half the student body—each\n                           year. Fall 2026 Career Fair Tuesday, September 29 Noon–5 p.m. Student Development Complex Career Fair for Students Career Fair for Employers Career Fest What kinds of things does your company bring to an industry trade show? Bring those\n                              same items to campus to show off to our students in an outdoor, casual event. This\n                              “show and tell” format lets students learn what you do or make and what kinds of jobs\n                              they can find at your company. Enhance your branding by participating in one or more\n                              of these days. Career Fest days are in the weeks leading up to the Career Fair. These events can\n                           be a useful part of your on-campus recruiting strategy. You don't need a suit or resume for Career Fest! We expect you to be dressed for class\n                           and will interact in a more informal setting. Interview Day The day after Career Fair, recruiters stick around to conduct thousands of interviews\n                           with our Huskies. Some students spend the whole day going from interview to interview.\n                           Faculty and staff donate office space to recruiters for the day to support our students. For Students Be prepared to interview right away, the day after Career Fair. Make sure you answer\n                                    calls from strange numbers on your phone Tuesday night–those might be recruiters calling\n                                    to schedule interviews. Also watch your texts and emails. Make sure you write down who is interviewing you when and where. Once you know who is interviewing you, do your homework on the employer(s). Make sure\n                                    you have a copy of your resume to bring with you. Think about how your resume relates\n                                    to the the employer's culture and business. Just like for Career Fair, make sure you dress professionally for your interview.\n                                    Make sure you set aside enough time to arrive at your interview location with time\n                                    to spare. Don't forget to send a Thank you note on Thursday. For Employers You can request interview spaces as an add-on when you register for Career Fair. Full-day and half-day options are available. Full-day interview spaces include lunch. You will have an opportunity to update your interview space request when you check\n                                       in for Career Fair. Interview space assignments will be published before or during Career Fair, so you\n                                    will be able to tell students where to meet you for their interviews. As you schedule interviews with students, please be sure to communicate your name, your company's name, and the location and\n                                       time of the interview. It is best to send them a text message, email, or calendar invitation. If the student\n                                    does not know these details, Career Services will not be able to help them find you. Career Services does not have information about employers' or students' interview\n                           schedules, nor does Career Services provide contact information for recruiters or\n                           students. You are responsible for your own schedule and obtaining any needed contact information. Virtual Fairs Virtual Career Fairs are a powerful way to augment your job search strategy. These\n                           events are often curated around specific majors, industries, or seasonal hiring trends , allowing you to connect with employers exactly when they are looking to hire. The Virtual Experience Unlike a traditional walk-up event, a virtual fair is built around a pre-arranged\n                           schedule. You begin by reviewing the list of participating employers in advance and\n                           selecting specific time slots that fit your schedule. These engagements typically\n                           range from 10-minute 1-on-1 chats to 30-minute group sessions conducted via a video conferencing system. As with any professional networking event, preparation is the key to success ; arriving with a polished resume and a clear \"elevator pitch\" will help you make\n                           a lasting impression during these focused conversations. See All Career Fairs Additional Resources Campus Map Campus Accessibility Map Career Events Career Fair News More News Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/events/": {
      "title": "Events",
      "description": "Events | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Events Events Career Services offers interactive events, both large and small, that connect students,\n                           employers, and alumni. Find additional career events and event details on Handshake and the Michigan Tech Events Calendar . Walk-in hours are available every Monday through Friday from 11 a.m. to 2 p.m. at\n                           the Career Services Learning Center. Career Fair Fair Our semi-annual career fair is open to all students and all majors. It is one of the\n                                          largest in the country, bringing more than 400 companies and 2,000 recruiters to campus\n                                          each year. The Fall 2026 Career Fair is Tuesday, September 29, 12–5 p.m., in the Student Development\n                                             Complex. Career Fest Fest Career Fest is a series of casual networking and recruiting events where companies\n                                          show off what they do to attract Huskies' attention. In the fall, these events are\n                                          held outside during the weeks leading up the Career Fair. Career Fest also includes\n                                          lightning resume review events where recruiters review and critique students' resumes. Upcoming Career Services Events See all events Subscribe to Michigan Tech Career Services events through Google Calendar or any other calendar program using the ICS format. Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/employers/": {
      "title": "Employers",
      "description": "Employers | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Employers Also in this section Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Employers How to Connect with Students Michigan Tech Career Services builds direct pathways between global industry leaders\n                              and tenacious Husky talent. We offer tailored recruitment structures ensuring organizations\n                              of every scale actively secure our highly driven student innovators. Register for Career Fair Additional Career Fair Events Getting Started We use Handshake to centralize all job postings, recruitment events, and corporate communications.\n                                             To recruit at Michigan Tech, your organization must maintain an active Employer Account . This single platform manages career fairs, information sessions, and campus-wide\n                                             event promotions. Job Postings Michigan Tech belongs to the global Handshake network, allowing you to cross-post open positions to multiple institutions simultaneously. Publishing your openings through this portal\n                                             ensures all students retain equitable access to your career paths. First-time users\n                                             should review our foundational platform documentation before posting. Post a Job Career Fairs The University-wide Career Fair fills the Student Development Complex every fall and\n                                          spring. This event brings more than 1,200 recruiters to campus, drawing 4,000 students\n                                          looking to solve tomorrow's complex challenges. While most departments participate\n                                          in this central fair, specific units like the College of Forest Resources and Environmental Science and the College of Business host independent, targeted recruiting events throughout the academic year. MTU Fall 2026 Career Fair will be Tuesday, September 29, 12 noon–5 p.m., in the Student\n                                          Development Complex. Register for Career Fair Additional Career Fair Opportunities Day Before All-Majors Career Fair Employers can maximize their time on campus by joining specialized events held on\n                                          the day preceding the main fair. The registration process automatically provides a\n                                          comprehensive list of these high-visibility engagement options. Registration Review Because we want your team to thrive, our Career Services staff personally reviews\n                                          every single registration that comes through our system. With so many fields to navigate—including\n                                          class years, job types, work authorization parameters, and specific majors—it is incredibly\n                                          easy to accidentally skip a field or leave a section blank. If we notice something\n                                          that seems to be missing or could use a bit more detail, don’t be surprised if our\n                                          team reaches out to you directly to clarify or update your registration. On Campus Interviews Career Services has interview rooms available for you to have private conversations\n                                       with our students. Facilities for virtual meetings can also be made available. If\n                                       you plan to do on-campus interviews, contact us at career@mtu.edu , and we will help you reserve a room and set up a schedule. If you are interviewing\n                                       our students virtually, remind them that we have spaces available for them. We also host Interview Day on the day after Career Fair. With your Career Fair registration,\n                                       you will be able to request an interview space on campus to interview the Huskies\n                                       you met at the fair in person. Career Fest Bring your physical products, raw materials, and industrial trade show displays directly\n                                          to campus. Held outdoors throughout September, this active demonstration format shows\n                                          Huskies exactly what your company makes and how your teams operate. Following these\n                                          outdoor sessions, employers review student resumes and build brand recognition directly\n                                          inside the Career Services Learning Center. Mid-summer registration guarantees your\n                                          space. Register for Career Fest Recruiting Events / Info Sessions Maximize student interaction by joining an existing, organized campus event. Organizations\n                                          may also build custom corporate presentations or virtual information sessions through Handshake . On-campus venue sourcing requires up to one week of lead time, particularly during\n                                          high-traffic weeks surrounding major fairs. Secure corporate catering directly through Michigan Tech Dining Services at least two weeks before your arrival. Calendars and Campus Events The Registrar maintains the official academic calendar . Recruiters tracking broader campus initiatives and local activities can view the\n                                          public events calendar . Career Education Workshops Our instructional staff conducts career readiness presentations throughout each academic\n                                          term. Pre-fair sessions focus exclusively on interview preparation, while post-fair\n                                          workshops cover networking and corporate professionalism. Experienced industry partners\n                                          can contact our team to serve as guest speakers or propose new professional development topics. Interview Rooms We provide private, professional offices designed to reduce student anxiety and facilitate\n                                          quiet conversation. These resources remain available for both in-person and virtual\n                                          interviews. Request your workspace by emailing your precise date, requested room count,\n                                          and representative names. Space remains highly limited during peak weeks. To request a space please email us at career@mtu.edu and be sure to include the following information: Date / Time Number of rooms Names of people coming Please visit our Michigan Tech Visitor/Pay-by-Use Parking page for information about where to park during your visit. Note: During extremely busy times around Career Fair, we have limited room available.\n                                        Additionally, Interview Rooms for the day after Career Fair are requested through\n                                       the Career Fair registration itself. Resume Books Michigan Tech does not distribute static resume books. We prioritize real-world interaction,\n                                          tracking student attendance digitally during live campus events to ensure organic,\n                                          data-driven professional connections. Sponsored student projects offer additional\n                                          avenues for direct digital networking. Classroom Presentations Academic faculty hold absolute authority over individual classroom schedules. Employers\n                                          seeking access to technical lectures must build authentic, long-term relationships\n                                          with professors to align corporate presentations directly with course learning objectives.\n                                          For broader institutional promotion, companies should leverage dedicated platforms\n                                          like Career Fest and the University-wide Career Fair. Campus Digital Advertising We promote corporate opportunities and brand placement through targeted digital advertising\n                                          displays. Employers can purchase these promotional structures during Career Fair registration\n                                          or when scheduling individual campus events. Our advertising packages leverage active\n                                          followings across major social platforms. Social Media Organizations can expand their recruiting footprint by tagging @mtucareer in corporate posts and stories. Utilizing official hashtags like #mtuJobs and #MTUCareerFair increases visibility among the student body. Paid multi-platform campaigns remain\n                                          available during fair registration. Student Organizations More than 200 Registered Student Organizations operate on campus. Employers can collaborate directly with relevant technical chapters\n                                          or sponsor their specific academic activities. Internships Many students complete professional internships during the summer term. Organizations\n                                          do not require external university approval to hire interns, and students face no\n                                          academic registration requirements for these roles. We survey participants at the\n                                          conclusion of their employment to document their real-world experiences. Note: Non-US citizens may require additional paperwork or documentation that the Co-op\n                                          program provides. Cooperative Education (Co-op) Co-op positions require a minimum commitment of one full academic semester, functioning\n                                          as a formalized partnership among the student, employer, and university. Students\n                                          earn active academic credit through a concurrent online course monitored by our staff. What Your Company Needs to Do: Maintain start and end dates that coincide within a window of time at the start and\n                                          end of our academic calendar Sign a Cooperative Education Agreement form provided by the student The supervisor will need to conduct two reviews per semester, the student will provide\n                                          the form and set up the meeting Suggestions for the Best Experience for the Student and Your Company Assign a mentor, who is not the supervisor, that the student will meet with on a regular\n                                          basis Have the students work on daily tasks and major projects Set up opportunities for socialization with co-workers and other students Have your students wrap up their experiences with a presentation Conduct an exit interview Co-op Requirements Undergraduate Students Minimum cumulative GPA 2.0 Must be in good academic and conduct standing Must receive permission from their academic advisor Must have completed at least one semester at Michigan Tech Graduate Students Minimum cumulative GPA 3.0 Must be in good academic and conduct standing Must receive permission from their academic or graduate advisor Must have completed at least one semester at Michigan Tech International Students: additional United States governmental requirements apply Must have completed two full time semesters in residence at Michigan Tech Must not have completed all degree requirements prior to co-op semesters Must obtain a Social Security Number from the Secretary of State Office Must have work authorization (CPT) Partner Program Joining the Career Services Partner Program gets you extra insights about recruiting\n                                       trends on our campus and shows your support for Huskies. Partner Program Benefits Current Partners Sponsorships Maximize your brand’s visibility and connect with Michigan Tech talent through these\n                                       high-impact sponsorship opportunities . Each package is designed to integrate your company into the student experience throughout\n                                       the Career Fair season. Event Communication We use Handshake as our exclusive communication pipeline. Students maintain active\n                                          profiles and specific career preferences inside this platform, which coordinates all\n                                          job postings, interview schedules, and event updates. Paying an Invoice When you register for an event, the \"Registrant\" will receive an email from Handshake\n                                       that includes a link to an invoice. The invoice includes a link that says \"Pay Here\"\n                                       in the bottom left corner. This link can be used to pay the invoice via credit card\n                                       directly online. If this doesn't work for you, please review the How to Pay for a Registration article. Getting Handshake Emails Delivered To ensure that the communications from Career Services that are generated by Handshake\n                                       get delivered to you, please review the How can I ensure deliverability article. Communication about future events, invoices, and details about your current\n                                       events will be sent from Handshake. Job Offer Guidelines As a member of the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE), We recommend\n                                       following the NACE guidelines for job offers. We ask that you provide realistic deadlines to students and follow up by the dates\n                                       that you promise during the interview process. Student Projects Engage students directly by sponsoring hands-on learning experiences through Senior Design and/or the Enterprise Program . You become the client and students work on your project for two academic semesters. Recruitment Expectations We adhere to the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Job Offer Guidelines and Principles for Ethical Professional Practice . Additional Resources Traveling to Tech Campus Map Degree Programs Career Services Events | Michigan Tech Events Employer Relations Team LinkedIn Jim Desrochers (he/him) Director, Employer Relations jtdesroc@mtu.edu 906-487-3461 Administration Building 220 Responsibilities Collaborates with employers to develop creative ways to connect with students Liaison to the Corporate Council LinkedIn Jill Patterson (she/her) Manager, Career and Employer Events jspatter@mtu.edu 906-487-3664 Administration Building 220 Responsibilities Manages Career Fair, Career Fest, and other career and employer events Manages Career Services materials and equipment Career Fair News Read More Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/employers/partner/benefits/": {
      "title": "Partner Program",
      "description": "Partner Program | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Employers Partner Program Also in this section Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Partner Program Career Services Partner Program (CSPP) Be part of the select group of companies that are highly active on campus and show\n                              your dedication to helping the next generation of Huskies be ready to enter the workforce. \n                              Our Partners help inform the events and programming we provide on campus, while helping students\n                              explore careers, develop professional skills, and connect with industry. What is the value of being a sponsor? Our sponsorship packages provide a platform for your organization to cultivate a sustainable\n                                          cycle of talent for the future by creating intentional recruitment strategies and\n                                          engagement with Michigan Tech students and alumni. Our staff works with your organization\n                                          to maximize the impact of campus outreach, to increase visibility and access to students,\n                                          and to provide consultation with Career Services staff. What do the levels of sponsorship include? There are four levels of sponsorship, all designed to provide a strategic recruiting\n                                          advantage for your organization through recruitment events, special programming, heightened\n                                          campus visibility and opportunities to build relationships with our campus community. Why should your organization become a sponsor? The return on investment outweighs the nominal costs of each sponsorship benefit by\n                                          providing intentional and effective services that best showcase your organization\n                                          and attract the large pool of talent that Michigan Tech has to offer. Sponsorship\n                                          provides a mechanism for employers to significantly streamline recruitment efforts,\n                                          grow talent and reduce resources needed to find the right talent, lowering overall\n                                          turnover. When can I sign up and how long will my sponsorship last? All sponsorships are accepted on an open-enrollment basis. Benefits are typically administered for\n                                          2 academic semesters - Fall and Spring of an academic year. Enrollment and invoicing in the CSPP, is managed through Handshake and the \"MTU Career\n                                          Services Sponsorship\" fair. Partner Benefits for 2026-2027 Updated April 8, 2026 Copper $2,500 Silver $5,000 Gold $10,000 Platinum $15,000 Branding Web Branding: Logo featured on the Career Services website ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Guest Speaking: Priority invitations for classroom and panel opportunities ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Early Access: First choice of workshops and student engagement events ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Social Media: Featured spotlights on our official social channels ✓ ✓ Handshake Exposure: Included in curated \"Employer Collections\" ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Digital Displays: Campus-wide slide rotation via the Electronic Display System (EDS) ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Graphic Support: Complimentary design and development of your EDS slides ✓ ✓ Signing Day: Professional recruitment photo at CAB or Design Expo ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Office Branding: Corporate logo displayed on a Career Services office ✓ ✓ Magazine Access: Advanced notice for Michigan Tech Magazine advertising ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Micro Info Sessions: Recruiting Videos shown in Quinncia ✓ ✓ ✓ All Majors Career Fair Guaranteed Early Pricing: Lock in \"Early Bird\" rates regardless of your registration date ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Career Fair Registration Fee - 1 Booth $1,250 ✓ ✓ ✓ Career Fair Registration Fee - 2 Booths $2,500 $1,250 ✓ ✓ Career Fair Registration Fee - 3 Booths $3,750 $2,500 $1,250 ✓ Priority Add-ons: Early access to purchase optional Career Fair enhancements ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Premium Placement: Secured booth location within the Multi-Purpose Room ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Map Visibility: Company name highlighted on the official Career Fair map ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Strategic Insights: Advanced notification regarding all upcoming recruiting events ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Exclusive Networking: Invitations to private pre-fair Department Mixers ✓ ✓ ✓ Interview Day: Complimentary Spots after Career Fair 2 free 3 free 4 free Unlimited Interview Space: Guaranteed post-fair interview spots in private or branded offices ✓ ✓ ✓ Recruiter Lounge: Exclusive access to the CSPP lounge during the fair ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Title Sponsorship: Naming rights for one Career Fair per year ✓ Career Fest Partner Preview: Exclusive access to the \"Partner Preview\" during Fall Partner Fest ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Fall Career Fest: Complimentary registrations 1 included 2 Included Unlimited Spring Career Fest: Early access to secure your spot before the general opening ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Hassle-Free Logistics: Campus parking passes for all your visits ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Consulting Priority Pre-Registration: Secure your spot first for all upcoming recruiting events ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Dedicated Collaboration: Partner with Employer Relations to maximize your program benefits ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Strategic Leadership: Seat on the Corporate Advisory Board (CAB) to influence campus recruiting ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Concierge Registration: Save time by letting us handle your event sign-ups for you ✓ ✓ Partner Program Contact LinkedIn Jim Desrochers (he/him) Director, Employer Relations jtdesroc@mtu.edu 906-487-3461 Administration Building 220 Responsibilities Collaborates with employers to develop creative ways to connect with students Liaison to the Corporate Council Partner Program News Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
