    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/faculty-staff/": {
      "title": "Faculty & Staff",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Faculty Faculty & Staff A campus career center is not the only resource that students turn to as they consider\n                           career options and readiness - they also look to faculty, staff, coaches, supervisors,\n                           and student organization advisors for guidance. No matter how many appointments, events,\n                           workshops, or career fairs we host, it’s important to recognize that faculty and staff are a key part of the career environment at Michigan Tech. Career Services has designed this page with the goal of equipping\n                           everyone across campus with the same set of resources to guide students on their career\n                           journeys. Career Services is here to help! Whether you’d like us to come to the classroom for\n                           a presentation, help you hire fantastic student-staff, or creatively brainstorm modules\n                           and activities for the classroom, our team is ready to collaborate. Presentations and Workshops Career in the Classroom Hire Huskies Career Readiness Competencies Everyone at Michigan Tech cares about the success of our students - not only during\n                                       their time in our programs, but also as they launch into the early stages of their\n                                       career. The work we do in Career Services is guided by the NACE Career Readiness Competencies , which employers and colleges have identified as the skills that set young professionals\n                                       up for the most success. Look familiar? Essential Education seeks to address many of the same topics as the NACE competencies. We are closely\n                                       aligned with Essential Ed, and work closely with their team to make sure that we are\n                                       all amplifying efforts, not reinventing wheels. As a campus community, we should all\n                                       seek to help students build, practice, and articulate these competencies. Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/faculty-staff/classroom/": {
      "title": "Integrating Career in the Classroom",
      "description": "Integrating Career in the Classroom | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Faculty Integrating Career in the Classroom Also in this section Faculty Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Integrating Career in the Classroom Whether your course has a formal professional development focus or not, there are\n                              frequent opportunities to bring career readiness into the classroom. This page is\n                              still under development, however a few initial resources that you may find beneficial\n                              are listed below. Presentations, Guest Speakers, and Workshops Of course, creating novel material takes extra bandwidth that you may not always have.\n                                       Career Services can certainly help by delivering a presentation or hosting a workshop\n                                       - visit our presentations page for more information and ideas of where to begin. If you don’t see the topic you\n                                       want, simply ask! We are happy to collaborate with you to build something that makes\n                                       the most sense for your students. Many departments also welcome alumni or other corporate recruiters to speak in class.\n                                       While Career Services does not presently do 1-to-1 matching of interested parties,\n                                       we are certainly happy to help when we are able to. If you have a corporate connection\n                                       that you plan to invite into the classroom, let us know! It helps our office understand\n                                       the rich network of involvement that our alumni stay connected with, and the many\n                                       ways in which they give back to current Huskies. New! Quinncia New for spring 2026, Career Services has brought on a tool called Quinncia - a resume and mock-interview review software that is available to students 24/7.\n                                       Supported by templates, feedback, and coaching examples from Career Services, as well\n                                       as running based on the same types of scanning software used by employers, Quinncia\n                                       provides helpful feedback to help students produce stronger job applications. Right now, use of Quinncia is open to instructors who wish to help us improve Quinncia’s\n                                       effectiveness by piloting it as part of a course, and to students who use it as an\n                                       appointment type through Career Services. If you’re interested in adding this tool\n                                       to a module in your course, let us know! Learn more about Quinncia’s resume and mock interview feedback processes through these linked overviews. Career Services Handouts For quick reference, the Students section of the Career Services website contains\n                                       easily printable materials that make easy launching-points for class conversations\n                                       around career topics. A few to consider include: Resume templates Personal introductions Interview basics LinkedIn profile tips Feel free to reach out to our team for questions or for guidance on how to use any\n                                       of these resources in the classroom. Canvas Resources Ready-to-deploy Canvas modules can be found in a few places. Career Services will\n                                       update this list as more resources are made available. Canvas Commons First, log in to Canvas, then navigate to Commons. Within, you can search “Michigan\n                                       Tech” and find resources including: Essential Education - Husky Life Success: Resume When adding these, you can make adjustments to your specific course as you see fit\n                                       - the module templates are provided by Career Services and Essential Ed as building\n                                       blocks. Don’t see what you need? Reach out to us and let’s discuss. For general Canvas help, reach out to the Center for Faculty Excellence . Coming Soon: PebblePad Workbooks Career Services is working in close collaboration with the Essential Education to\n                                       develop templates and workbooks to be deployed via Husky Folio (on the PebblePad platform). As these become available, we will list examples and\n                                       provide guidance on integrating them here. In the meantime, if you have ideas for workbooks or templates that you would find\n                                       useful, send us a note at career@mtu.edu so that we can start a conversation. Contact Us Liz Fujita (she/her) Assistant Director, Academic and Career Integration liz@mtu.edu 906-487-1161 Administration Building 220 Melissa Michaelson (she/her) Assistant Director, Career Development and Education mmichael@mtu.edu 906-487-2570 Administration Building 220 Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/events/presentations/": {
      "title": "Presentations",
      "description": "Presentations | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Events Presentations & Workshops Presentations Don't Cancel Class! Going to a conference and need a class session covered? This is another opportunity\n                              to invite Career Services to the classroom in your absence. We'll work with you by\n                              request to shape a presentation topic around the specific needs of your class, major,\n                              or focus area. Plan ahead, send us a request to discuss, and let’s see what we can\n                              create together. Career Services offers presentations for groups on campus including classes and student\n                           organizations. We can present to your group on a variety of career-related topics. For a change of scenery, we are also happy to host groups of up to 25 in our office ( Administration Building 220 ). Please give us a minimum of one week's notice for all events. We will make every effort\n                           to work with you and fulfill your request, but we cannot guarantee availability with less than one week's notice or for events scheduled to take place after 5 p.m. Request a Group Presentation Presentations Offered AI and the Job Search (50 minutes) Discover how AI is transforming the job search and hiring process and how it affects\n                                       the way opportunities are found and talent is recognized. We will explore practical\n                                       strategies for utilizing AI effectively and responsibly. Career Fair Prep (50 minutes) Is there more to Career Fair than bringing a few copies of my resume? Absolutely,\n                                       and with a plan, there is a much higher chance of reaching your career fair goals. Cover Letters (25 minutes) Cover letters may be the determining factor in the final decision. The key is quality\n                                       over quantity. We will discuss strategies to ensure the cover letter shows a clear\n                                       match between the student and the job/company. Experiential Learning Opportunities (50 minutes) Explore how co-ops, internships, classroom projects, student organizations, informational\n                                       interviews, and job shadowing can unlock opportunities, build your skills, and set\n                                       you apart in your career journey. Discover how these experiences can help you stand\n                                       out to employers. How to Use Handshake (30 minutes) We'll show students how to get the most out of Handshake, including job search, career\n                                       fair, and career events. Interview Basics (25 minutes) Tips and tricks on how to be prepared and present your best self during an interview,\n                                       including the STAR method. Interviews in Depth (50 minutes) Same as above and includes example questions and how to answer them. Job Offer Evaluation and Negotiation (25 minutes) Congrats, you got the offer! Ensure you have the tools to evaluate and negotiate (if\n                                       and when you should). Job Search Strategies and Resources (25 minutes) Only 20% of jobs are posted on the internet. Students will learn skills and strategies\n                                       for an effective search. Search smarter, not harder. Unlock possibilities, and create\n                                       an action plan that will get you going. Personal Branding, Networking, and LinkedIn (50 minutes) Connections = Opportunities Many underestimate the power of an introduction. When asked, “Tell me about yourself,”\n                                       what do they really want to know? Is networking as scary as it seems? It doesn't have\n                                       to be. 94% of recruiters use LinkedIn to vet candidates. Is your profile ready? Students\n                                       will learn how to write an effective summary, key profile components, and how to make\n                                       LinkedIn work for you. Reflection, Exploration, and Goal Setting (50 minutes) You have to start somewhere. Figure out how to leverage your strengths and improve\n                                       upon weaknesses to prepare for your future. Resume Basics (25 minutes) A recruiter may only spend five seconds looking at a resume. We will review the content\n                                       and organization necessary for an effective resume. Resumes: Beyond the Basics (50 minutes) More employers are hiring based on candidates' skills. This presentation describes\n                                       what a skills-based resume is and how to make one. Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/faculty-staff/champions/": {
      "title": "Career Champions",
      "description": "Career Champions | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Faculty Career Champions Also in this section Faculty Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Career Champions Student career readiness is one of the core elements of our work in Career Services\n                              - but, we know we are not alone. Many others across campus, both as a direct function\n                              of their role on campus and as people who care about Huskies, are deeply committed\n                              to ensuring that students find success in their pre-professional growth. Nationwide,\n                              the movement toward a career ecosystem model is growing: when career readiness is integrated in classrooms, advising conversations,\n                              RSO leadership development, and elsewhere across the academic experience, it demonstrates\n                              a campus-wide investment in success. The Career Champions program is intended to give faculty and staff the background\n                              knowledge to support students with a wide range of career-related topics and make\n                              appropriate referrals to Career Services when needed. Register for Upcoming Workshops Current Career Champions Name Title Department Nicholas Ambs Coordinator of Admissions Operations Admissions Natalie Anderson Manager, Advising and Cooperative Education Career Services Kirsti Arko Associate Director Admissions Breann Baker Regional Admissions Manager Admissions Maria Bergstrom Associate Dean for Undergraduate Education College of Sciences and Arts Rick Berkey Senior Research Innovation Specialist Vice President of Research Office Jaylen Body Visit Coordinator Admissions Tara Brewer Regional Admissions Manager Admissions Ninette Carlson Assistant Director of Admissions Admissions Stephanie Carpenter Associate Professor of Creative Writing and Literature Humanities Deb Charlesworth Associate Dean of Graduate Student Success Dean of Students Marie Cleveland Student Success and Outreach Coordinator College of Business Jeana Collins Teaching Professor Chemical Engineering Jim Desrochers Director, Employer Relations Career Services Beth Fitzpatrick Senior Career Advisor Career Services Lauren Flanagan Assistant Director of Admissions Admissions Elka Frahm General Manager Merchandising Operations Alyssa Fredin Executive Director Admissions Liz Fujita Assistant Director, Academic & Career Integration Career Services Chrissy Grotzke Sr. Associate Director of Admissions Admissions Tom Hampton Regional Admissions Manager Admissions Claire Helakoski Assistant Writing Center Director Writing Center Elijah Hopp Enrollment Communications Coordinator Enrollment Management Alex Hughes Data & Technology Specialist Career Services Kristi Juntunen Honors Program Manager Pavlis Honors College Cody Kangas Executive Director Career Services Julia Keleher Director Student Support and Mentorship Madeline Kilps Senior Administrative Aide Admissions Brianna Kratz Assistant Director of Residence Education Residence Education Matt Laird Academic Advisor Geological and Mining Engineering and Sciences Denise Landsberg Academic Advisor College of Computing Betsy Lehman Visiting Assistant Professor Psychology and Human Factors Jon Leinonen Teaching Professor College of Business Susan Liebau Academic Advisor Chemistry Kate Marin Academic Advisor Electrical and Computer Engineering Lea Marlor Graduate Academic Coordinator title=\"Graduate School\">Graduate School Danielle Meirow Director Student Leadership and Involvement Melissa Michaelson Assistant Director, Career Development and Education Career Services Jennifer Miller Program Chair/Professor of Practice Construction Management Alice Morgan Associate Director Admissions Dar Morris Assistant Dean Pavlis Honors College Jenni Nance Assistant Teaching Professor & Faculty Advisor Humanities Jessie Neece Marketing & Communications Manager Office of the Associate Provost for Undergraduate Education David Olson Associate Teaching Professor Mathematical Sciences AC Overla Residence Education Coordinator Residence Education Steve Patchin Project Manager, Essential Education Implementation Office of the Associate Provost for Undergraduate Education Jill Patterson Manager, Career and Employer Events Career Services Taylor Piering Coordinator Student Leadership and Involvement Cole Pierucki Senior Coordinator Student Leadership and Involvement Tony Pinar Associate Teaching Professor Electrical and Computer Engineering Teri Pinhero Academic Advisor Biological Sciences Alexandra Putwen Director of Residence Education Residence Education Cassandra Reed-VanDam Essential Education Experience Manager APUE Thomas Schlitt Associate Director of International & Transfer Admissions Admissions Stefanie Sidortsova Manager, Strategic Communications Career Services Sarah Sohlden Aerospace Engineering Advisor Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Marina Stack Regional Admissions Manager Admissions Ryan Thompson Communications Specialist Student Affairs Jennifer Todd Regional Admissions Manager Admissions Ali Tuovila Administrative Aide Career Services Micah Vacco Coordinator Student Leadership and Involvement Jennifer Van Essen Regional Admissions Manager Admissions Travis Wakeham Associate Teaching Professor Biological Sciences Richelle Winkler Professor of Sociology and Demography Social Sciences LaReesa Wolfenbarger Dean, College of Sciences and Arts College of Sciences and Arts Roger Woods Teaching Professor College of Business Sherry Wyeth Academic Advisor and Graduate Program Assistant College of Computing By completing this training, participants will be able to: Understand, explain, and actively participate in the career ecosystem at Michigan\n                                 Tech. Answer student questions regarding resources, workshops , events , employers , and career exploration. Recognize new trends and best practices pertaining to internships/ co-ops , resumes, interviewing, and negotiations. Identify which career competencies they can best support and develop in students. Being a member of the Career Champions entails: An in-person training workshop (approx. 2.5 hours) covering topics including: Resume, cover letter, and interview best practices Walk-throughs of key platforms ( Handshake , Quinncia) NACE career readiness competencies AI in the job search How employers recruit and engage with Huskies Receiving a bi-weekly digest with event updates, continuing education, articles, and\n                                 other career-related content. Active engagement with Career Services events Having their name and department listed on Career Services website Career Services supports members by providing: Access to continuing career readiness education through “booster pack” sessions and\n                                 regular newsletter updates Access to data and insights regarding student outcomes (First Destination Survey results,\n                                 placement forecasts, etc.) Access to a dedicated Canvas course with resources, links, templates, handouts, and\n                                 videos. Direct collaboration on projects such as course content, classroom presentations and\n                                 workshops, and other events specific to the student audience the Champions serve. Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/alumni/": {
      "title": "Resources for Alumni",
      "description": "Resources for Alumni | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Alumni Resources for Alumni As an alum, you are eligible to take advantage of all of the same services you had\n                              access to as a student. Find more detailed information below. Professional Assistance One-on-one advising appointments. Get help with your resume, cover letter, LinkedIn\n                                             profile, job search or networking skills, and career changes. Schedule a phone or\n                                             virtual appointment via Handshake , email career@mtu.edu, or call 906-487-2313. Access to Handshake , the latest job search technology, featuring a job board with hundreds of new jobs\n                                             posted daily, as well as contact information for recruiting companies. Learn what Handshake can do for you after graduation . Participate in any of our Career Fair events. Networking Meet fellow alumni and friends in your area. Check the list of regional Alumni Events ! Social network groups (see below) Alumni-student networking International alumni Be sure to connect with Alumni Engagement to learn more or email them with your questions at alumni@mtu.edu . Facebook Linkedin Recruiting Your employer can connect to Michigan Tech to post positions or actively recruit on\n                                             campus. If you'd like to highlight a job at your company to other Alumni, we recommend you\n                                             post it in the LinkedIn Alumni group . If you have a job posted in Handshake that you'd like to highlight, please email the\n                                             URL of the Handshake job posting to careerfair@mtu.edu and ask us to highlight it in the \"By Huskies For Huskies\" collection. Volunteering We are always looking for Alumni who are willing to help our existing students with\n                                       mentoring, guidance, and advice.  If you'd like to be added to our list of volunteers,\n                                       please email career@mtu.edu . First Destination Survey Graduating Students – What’s Next for You? When you were graduating, you probably received a few emails about the First Destination\n                                       Survey. Now it's your turn to help us tell the next chapter of the Michigan Tech story. By sharing your post-graduation plans, you’re helping us showcase the incredible accomplishments\n                                       of our Husky grads. Whether you’ve accepted a job, are continuing your education,\n                                       or still exploring options, your response matters. This data plays a crucial role in demonstrating the real-world value of a Michigan\n                                       Tech education to prospective students, families, and employers. Thank you for having taken time to complete the survey.  If you graduated in the past\n                                       6 months and haven't filled it out yet - there's still time!  Check your email and\n                                       complete the survey today. Career Services Resources for Alumni Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/career/connect/": {
      "title": "About Us",
      "description": "About Us | Career Services Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Career Services Career Services Connect Also in this section Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge About Us Michigan Tech Career Services collaborates with employers, alumni, faculty, and staff\n                           to connect students with opportunities and support all Huskies on their career journeys.\n                           We provide career education and guidance for students and alumni, administer the Cooperative\n                           Education Program, and host numerous events every semester, including a giant career\n                           fair, to give our students and employers the opportunity to connect. Location and Hours Administration Building ( Campus Map , Building 1) Suite 220 Open Monday-Friday Hours: 8 a.m.–5 p.m. (fall and spring semesters) | 8 a.m.–4 p.m. (summer) Contact Information Phone: 906-487-2313 Fax: 906-487-3317 Email: career@mtu.edu Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://blogs.mtu.edu/career/": {
      "title": "Career Services Blog",
      "description": "Career Services Blog Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Students Faculty/Staff Alumni Parents Industry Tech Links A to Z Banweb Campus Map Canvas Email MyMichiganTech Safety Data Sheets Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Directory Go Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Blog Programs Directory Search Students Resumes and Letters Networking and Interviews Jobs | Co-ops | Internships Start Your Career Path On-Campus Jobs Career Fair Events Employers How to Hire Huskies Partner Program Current Employer Partners Career Fair Faculty/Staff Integrating Career in the Classroom Presentations On-Campus Jobs Career Champions Alumni Career Fair Events Connect Career Services Blog Staff Listing Data Portrait Lounge Info For . . . Students Faculty/Staff Alumni Parents Tech Links A to Z Banweb Campus Map Canvas Email MyMichiganTech Safety Data Sheets Career Services Blog Fall 2026 – Pre-Fair Events Stickied By Jim Desrochers Career Fair Employer Recruiting We know that when you travel to campus, every hour counts. If you want to get the absolute most out of your visit, the night before the Career Fair is your golden opportunity to build meaningful connections with students before the main event. To help you maximize your time on campus, we highly recommend adding these high-impact engagement options to your itinerary when you register for the Career Fair or finalize your travel arrangements. Enhance Your Presence: Targeted Campus Mixers As part of your registration process, you can opt-in to receive invitations to our campus Mixers . These are highly targeted, department-hosted networking events designed to connect you with smaller, specific groups of students. Continue Reading → Fall 2026 Career Fest Schedule Stickied By Career Services Career Fair Employer Recruiting Are you concerned that students won’t recognize your brand?  Career Fest events allow you to highlight the things you make and do! What kinds of things does your company bring to an industry trade show? Bring those same items to campus to show off to our students in an outdoor, casual event. This “show and tell” format lets students learn what you do or make and what kinds of jobs they can find at your company. Enhance your branding by participating in one or more of these days. The lineup for Fall 2026 includes: Thu, Sep 4 | $75 | Local Jobs Expo (Employers in Baraga, Houghton, and Keweenaw Counties) Wed, Sep 9 | $550 | Michigan Day (Employers with an office in Michigan) Tue, Sep 15 | $550 | General Industry Day Thu, Sep 17 | $550 | General Industry Day Tue, Sep 22 | $550 | Foundry Fest Wed, Sep 23 | $0 | Aerospace Day (Employers in the Aerospace Industry) Continue Reading → Navigating Pre-Employment Drug Screenings Published June 15, 2026 By Career Services Recruiting Securing a conditional job offer for an internship, co-op, or full-time position is an exciting milestone! However, before you can officially cross the finish line and start your first day, many employers will require you to complete a pre-employment drug screening as part of their hiring policy. To help you seamlessly navigate this step of the onboarding process, the team at Michigan Tech Career Services has broken down what to expect, industry standards, and how to handle testing logistics from our unique location in the Keweenaw. Continue Reading → Employer Tips: Finding the “Right” Fair for Your Hiring Organization Published June 15, 2026 By Jim Desrochers Career Fair Employer Recruiting Now, more than ever, a successful university recruiting strategy needs to be intentional. Simply showing up on campus is no longer enough—you need to align your presence with your specific hiring goals, target demographics, and capacity. At Michigan Tech, we organize a diverse portfolio of events throughout the academic year to maximize your brand exposure and ensure high-quality interactions with our students. To help you build the most effective recruiting calendar, we’ve broken down the primary ways you can connect with Huskies, and how to determine which options are the right match for your business. Continue Reading → How to Identify and Avoid Job Market Scams Published June 9, 2026 By Career Services Career Education As you navigate the job market looking for internships, co-ops, or full-time roles, it is vital to stay vigilant. Online scammers frequently pose as legitimate employers in order to defraud students. These scams can be incredibly difficult to identify, but keeping a few key safety practices in mind will help keep your search secure. At Michigan Tech Career Services, your professional safety is our top priority. Use this guide to recognize the red flags, protect your data, and safeguard your job search. 1. Recognize the Red Flags: When an Offer is “Too Good to Be True” Employment scams often prey on a student’s need for flexible, high-paying work. Understanding the anatomy of a scam is your first line of defense. The Financial Hook: A legitimate employer will never ask you to pay money upfront, process financial transactions, or purchase equipment with the promise of reimbursement. Watch out for “check-cashing” or “task” scams, where an employer sends you a large check, asks you to deposit it, and requests that you wire or transfer a portion back (via Venmo, cryptocurrency, or gift cards). Once the bank discovers the scammer’s check is fraudulent, you will be held legally and financially responsible for those missing funds. Over-Urgency and Minimal Vetting: Be wary of recruiters who extend an immediate job offer without a formal interview or background check. Scammers often use language that creates a false sense of urgency (“Immediate start,” “Reply within 24 hours”) to bypass your critical thinking. Vague Roles with Sky-High Pay: If a posting promises $500 a week for minimal, unstructured remote work—such as a “virtual assistant” or “data entry clerk”—but completely neglects to mention core job responsibilities, proceed with extreme caution. Text and Chat-Only Hiring: Legitimate organizations require thorough vetting. If the entire interview and hiring process takes place solely via text message, WhatsApp, Telegram, or Google Hangouts, refuse to move forward until you can secure a video or in-person interview. Continue Reading → Career Fair Registration Review Process Published May 29, 2026 By Jim Desrochers Career Fair Employer Recruiting We truly appreciate your investment in recruiting at Michigan Tech. Whether you are looking for your next engineering co-op or a full-time business analyst, our goal is to ensure you have the best, most productive experience possible throughout the entire process. A successful campus visit starts long before you set up your booth—it begins the moment you submit your registration details. Because we want your team to thrive, our Career Services staff personally reviews every single registration that comes through our system. With so many fields to navigate—including class years, job types, work authorization parameters, and specific majors—it is incredibly easy to accidentally skip a field or leave a section blank. If we notice something that seems to be missing or could use a bit more detail, don’t be surprised if our team reaches out to you directly to clarify or update your registration. This thorough review process is entirely for your benefit. When thousands of Huskies begin researching employers in the weeks leading up to the fair, they don’t just scroll through a massive list alphabetically. Instead, they use advanced filters to narrow down the playing field. Students search for very specific criteria to identify exactly which companies they need to visit, matching their current status and future goals to your open roles. If your registration parameters aren’t clearly specified, your company might accidentally become invisible to your target audience. For example, if you are looking for sophomore interns but forget to select “Internship” or “Sophomore” in your registration dropdowns, your booth won’t show up when a sophomore filters for summer internships. By keeping your data precise and complete, you ensure that the right students can easily find you. Think of your career fair registration as your digital storefront. Taking an extra five minutes to meticulously review your job types, target majors, and open positions ensures that the algorithm works for you, not against you. We are excited to host you on campus soon, and we look forward to working together to make this your most successful recruiting season yet! Continue Reading → Local Jobs Expo 2026 Published May 27, 2026 By Jim Desrochers Career Fair Employer Recruiting The Local Jobs Expo is designed exclusively for employers with offices located in Baraga, Houghton, and Keweenaw counties. This event highlights the valuable career opportunities available within our region while strengthening connections between local employers, Michigan Tech students, and the surrounding community. By participating, your organization helps support the growth and retention of talent in the local community and showcases the many ways students can build meaningful careers in the Copper Country. If your organization is interested in connecting with Michigan Tech students and providing professional development opportunities, we encourage you to participate. Students are eager to learn about local part-time employment, full-time career opportunities, and job shadowing experiences within our community. This fair will be held on Friday, September 4, 2026 .  (Registration is part of our Career Fest series of events.) Continue Reading → 2026 Signing Day Published April 21, 2026 By Career Services Employer Recruiting Student Stories We took advantage of a sunny spring day in Houghton to celebrate our students with a “Signing Day” photo session at the Husky statue. This event serves as a visual testament to the hard work and dedication our students put into their professional development. Whether embarking on a summer internship, a semester-long co-op, or a full-time career after graduation, these Huskies are ready to make a significant impact in their respective fields. It is an exciting time on campus as we watch these students launch into their next chapters. These photos represent more than just a job placement; they represent the culmination of a rigorous Michigan Tech education and the bright futures that lie ahead. We are incredibly proud to see our students joining industry leaders and innovators across the country. Continue Reading → Employer Tips: How to Maximize Results at Virtual Career Fairs Published April 3, 2026 By Jim Desrochers Career Fair Employer Recruiting Virtual career fairs have shifted from a “backup plan” to a powerful, permanent tool in the recruiter’s arsenal. While the preparation might feel lighter than hauling booths and banners across the country, achieving a high ROI requires a shift in strategy. Success in the digital space isn’t about just showing up—it’s about intentional action. Here are suggestions to help turn virtual sessions into hires. Continue Reading → How to Complete Your Handshake Profile Published February 27, 2026 By Career Services Handshake Tips Handshake helps you find job opportunities by matching your profile with roles that align with your interests and experience. The more complete your profile is, the better it can deliver relevant and personalized job recommendations. Here are the steps to get you started. Activate Your Account Simply log in to Handshake using your standard SSO credentials. Complete Your Profile Handshake will guide you through the process of adding details about the types of jobs you’re seeking and the work experience you bring.  For more details about the process, please review the Completing Your Profile in Handshake article. Profile Picture You can use the photo booth in Career Services to get a professional profile picture in less than 15 minutes. Download The Handshake App You can use Handshake from your desktop, but you might find it more convenient to use it on your mobile device.  The Handshake app is available on both Android and iOS . Learn more about what you can do on the Handshake Mobile app. Continue Reading → 1 2 3 4 | Next | Last Subscribe Categories Categories Select Category Alumni  (4) Announcements  (3) Career Education  (3) Career Fair  (12) Data  (3) Employer  (13) Handshake Tips  (11) Recruiting  (12) Student Stories  (2) Latest Posts Navigating Pre-Employment Drug Screenings Employer Tips: Finding the “Right” Fair for Your Hiring Organization How to Identify and Avoid Job Market Scams Career Fair Registration Review Process Fall 2026 – Pre-Fair Events Fall 2026 Career Fest Schedule Michigan Tech Industry News Michigan Tech Researchers Develop Sustainable Building Material from Wood Waste Mechatronics at Michigan Tech: More Than Machines Through Industry Partnerships, HuskyWorks Develops First-ever Lunar Road College of Engineering News MTU Mechanical Engineering Research Team Selected for NASA Space Habitat Challenge M. Emin Kutay Named Department of Civil, Environmental, and Geospatial Engineering Chair From Campus to Cosmos: MTU Astro-Huskies Place Third in NASA Lunabotics Challenge Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Degrees / Majors Colleges and Departments Library Events Calendar Arts and Entertainment Fitness and Recreation Campus and Beyond Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Athletics Campus Map Campus Directory Jobs at Michigan Tech Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Career Services Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, Michigan 49931 906-487-2313 906-487-3317 career@mtu.edu Instagram Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Blog with WordPress Tomorrow Needs Michigan Tech © 2026 Michigan Technological University"
    },
