      "title": "Dean of Students",
      "description": "Dean of Students Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Safety and Emergency Resources Student Emergency Support Health Alerts Student Support and Resources Health and Medical Care HuskyFAN Food Pantry Academic Support Where To Go For What Parents Fund Experience Tech Free Speech Pregnant and Parenting Students Religious and Cultural Resources Policies and Procedures Academic Forms Curriculum Add/Drop First-Year Student Drop/Add Overload Permission Release of Information Petition for a Third and Final Attempt at a Course Student Withdrawal Who We Are Mission, Vision, Goals Values Statement Staff Listing Contact Us Report a Concern Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Safety and Emergency Resources Student Emergency Support Health Alerts Student Support and Resources Health and Medical Care HuskyFAN Food Pantry Academic Support Where To Go For What Parents Fund Experience Tech Free Speech Pregnant and Parenting Students Religious and Cultural Resources Policies and Procedures Academic Forms Curriculum Add/Drop First-Year Student Drop/Add Overload Permission Release of Information Petition for a Third and Final Attempt at a Course Student Withdrawal Who We Are Mission, Vision, Goals Values Statement Staff Listing Contact Us Report a Concern Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Dean of Students Helping Students Find Success The Dean of Students Office is a resource center for all Michigan Tech students. Our goal is to guide, support,\n                        and, on occasion, challenge students in their academic and personal endeavors. Student\n                        success is at the heart of our work. Student Emergency Resources Absence Request Form News from the Dean Emergency: Dial 911 Common ways the Dean of Students Office can help: Provide guidance and interventions for students and families during personal emergencies\n                              or difficult circumstances Provide consultation to faculty and staff regarding student issues or concerns Respond to general student issues and concerns Advocate for students Support and guide students through policies and procedures Dean's List Learn More Emergency Resources Learn More Attendance Policy and Absence Form Learn More Counseling Services Title IX We Are Here to Help Request a meeting with the Dean of Students by emailing deanofstudents@mtu.edu or by visiting the Waino Wahtera Center for Student Success, Room 130, in the Administration and Student Services Building . Kellie Raffaelli, EdD Associate Vice President for Student Affairs Dean of Students kraffael@mtu.edu 906-487-2212 Administration Building 130 Tiffany Jaeger Manager of Student Outreach and Retention tiffanyj@mtu.edu 906-487-2212 Admin Building - room 130 Rachel Colling Senior Administrative Aide rlamere@mtu.edu 906-487-2212 Administration Building - room 130 Quick Links Absence Request Form Change your Major/Minor/Concentration First-year Student Permission to Add/Drop Courses Form Overload Permission Form Third Attempt Form Husky Family Den Hours Monday–Friday Academic Year 8 a.m.–5 p.m. Summer 8 a.m.–4 p.m. After Hours and Weekends Email us. Make an Appointment Phone 906-487-2212 Email deanofstudents@mtu.edu Location Administration and Student Services Building Waino Wahtera Center for Student Success, Room 130 Request an Absence The University expects students to attend all scheduled class times unless an absence\n                                 is excused under the attendance policy . For absences of 3 or more days or if you missed a major assignment, exam, or other\n                                    graded requirement of the class, you may request an excused absence by completing\n                                    the Absence Request Form. If your absence is fewer than 3 days, please work directly with your instructor to make arrangements for making up the work you missed. Events View More Try something new. Make connections. Think differently. Grow. Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Dean of Students Administration Building 130 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, MI 49931-1295 906-487-2212 906-487-3060 deanofstudents@mtu.edu Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
    "https://www.mtu.edu/jobs/": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities Skip to page content Skip to footer navigation Menu Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Go Undergraduate Admissions Majors, Minors, and More Cost and Financial Aid Visit Campus Request Information Admitted Students Transfer to Michigan Tech Apply to Michigan Tech Graduate Admissions Prospective Students On-Campus Degrees and Certificates Online Degrees and Certificates Financial Information Request Information Admitted Students Apply to Michigan Tech Academics Majors, Degrees, and Programs Colleges and Departments Accreditation Pavlis Honors College Library Career Services Enterprise Program Campus Life Athletics Housing and Dining Life at Tech Recreation Student Leadership and Involvement Student Mental Health and Well-being Webcams Research R1 at Michigan Tech Research Areas Current Research Projects Centers and Institutes Research Stats and Data Undergraduate Research About University Facts and Figures Jobs at Michigan Tech History Traditions Michigan Tech Magazine Michigan Tech News President's Council Search Clear Search Input Search Category Michigan Tech This Site Programs Search Undergraduate Admissions Majors, Minors, and More Cost and Financial Aid Visit Campus Request Information Admitted Students Transfer to Michigan Tech Apply to Michigan Tech Graduate Admissions Prospective Students On-Campus Degrees and Certificates Online Degrees and Certificates Financial Information Request Information Admitted Students Apply to Michigan Tech Academics Majors, Degrees, and Programs Colleges and Departments Accreditation Pavlis Honors College Library Career Services Enterprise Program Campus Life Athletics Housing and Dining Life at Tech Recreation Student Leadership and Involvement Student Mental Health and Well-being Webcams Research R1 at Michigan Tech Research Areas Current Research Projects Centers and Institutes Research Stats and Data Undergraduate Research About University Facts and Figures Jobs at Michigan Tech History Traditions Michigan Tech Magazine Michigan Tech News President's Council Connect with Us Request Info Visit Apply Give Resources for You Prospective Students Admitted Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents and Family Industry and Partners Tech Links A to Z Campus Directory Canvas Concur Email Experience Safety Data Sheets Website Settings Employment Opportunities Home Employment Opportunities Welcome home Welcome to the banks of the largest freshwater lake in the world, to national parks,\n                        deep history, and thousands of acres of forestland. Welcome to four seasons and year-round\n                        adventures. Welcome to the Copper Country. The community. Campus. Welcome to Michigan Tech . Find Your Job Professional Employment Learn More Faculty and Staff Vacancies Partner Engagement Program Chamber of Commerce Job Search Keweenaw Information Student Employment Learn More Work-Study Programs Co-ops and Internships Campus and Community Employment Career Services Welcome to Michigan Technological University Michigan Technological University is located in Michigan's Upper Peninsula. Houghton overlooks the Keweenaw (say \"Kee-Wah-Nah\") Waterway and is just a few miles from\n                        Lake Superior. The area's waters, forests, and snowfall (215\" on average annually)\n                        offer skiing, snowboarding, hiking, biking, and paddling opportunities. Home to 12,000\n                        residents and active with locally owned shops, eateries, high-tech companies, music\n                        festivals, and parades, Michigan Tech and the Copper Country have a small-town feel.\n                        Students and community members say it's just right—not so big that it's easy to get\n                        lost, but not too small, either. We embrace our size, climate, sense of adventure,\n                        and originality. Michigan Tech wouldn't be the same anywhere else on earth—and we\n                        wouldn't have it any other way. An ideal place to call home. The Copper Country Learn More The Community Learn More The Campus Learn More Virtual Tours Virtual Tour Explore Campus Map Explore Join Husky Nation Admissions Grad School MTU Jobs Thinking of Relocating to the Keweenaw? Michigan Technological University is located in Houghton . Michigan Tech and the Copper Country have a small-town feel. Students and community\n                                 members say it’s just right—not so big that it’s easy to get lost, but not too small,\n                                 either. An ideal place to call home, Niche.com ranks Michigan Tech one of the safest public colleges in Michigan. The area is home to 12,000 residents, and active with locally owned shops, eateries,\n                                 high-tech companies, music festivals, and parades. Students, staff, and the community\n                                 enjoy the University-owned ski, snowboard, and tubing hill , golf course , and recreation trails , and other outdoor adventure opportunities the Keweenaw Peninsula offers. Apply for Admission Michigan Tech Jobs Helpful Links Local Jobs Partner Engagement Program Keweenaw Information Public Schools Child Care: Little Huskies | BHK | Great Start Collaborative City of Houghton Houghton County Real Estate More Community Info Request Information Schedule a Visit Give Apply Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Global Campus Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Virtual Tours Study and Live Academics Degrees / Majors Library Athletics Campus and Beyond Events Calendar Recreation Campus Info About Michigan Tech Accreditation Campus Map Jobs at Michigan Tech News Summer Youth Programs Webcams Policies and Safety Campus Safety Information Emergency Contact Information Report a Concern Public Safety / Police Services Student Disclosures Title IX University Policies Michigan Technological University 1400 Townsend Drive, Houghton, Michigan 49931-1295 906-487-1885 Facebook Instagram Snapchat Twitter Linkedin Youtube Accessibility Equal Opportunity Email the Webmaster © 2026 Michigan Technological University ©"
    },
