    "https://www.linkedin.com/company/mtu-career-services": {
      "title": "Michigan Tech Career Services",
      "description": "Michigan Tech Career Services | LinkedIn Skip to main content LinkedIn Top Content People Learning Jobs Games Sign in Join now Michigan Tech Career Services Higher Education Houghton, MI 1,682 followers Career Services collaborates with employers, alumni, faculty, and staff to connect students with opportunities. Follow Discover all 5 employees Report this company About us Michigan Tech Career Services collaborates with employers, alumni, faculty, and staff to connect students with opportunities and support all Huskies on their career journeys.\n\nAppointments with career advisors may be scheduled through Handshake and walk-ins with peer career coaches are available 11 a.m. - 1 p.m. Monday-Friday.\n\nhttps://mtu.joinhandshake.com/login Website www.mtu.edu/career/ External link for Michigan Tech Career Services Industry Higher Education Company size 1,001-5,000 employees Headquarters Houghton, MI Type Educational Founded 1885 Locations Primary Administration Building 220 1400 Townsend Drive Houghton, MI 49931, US Get directions Employees at Michigan Tech Career Services McDonald Masaze Lorelei George Madelyn Applekamp See all employees Updates Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Handshake 193,273 followers 4d Report this post 48 career centers have trusted Handshake for 11 or 12 years to help their students land jobs that launch their careers. Think about what that means: over a decade of showing up for students together and evolving to meet their needs. \n\nPartnerships like these are earned, day by day. To all 48 of our more-than-a-decade partners: thank you for your years of trust, and for pushing us to be better every single year. 💙 👇Check out these schools and tag your team if you spot your name! #CareerServices #HigherED Aquinas College, Eastern Michigan University, Hillsdale College, Adelphi University, Adrian College, Bates College, Baylor University, Brandeis University, Butler University, Canisius College, Colorado State University - Fort Collins, Cornell University, Cornerstone University, Davidson College, Denison University, DePaul University, Drexel University, Gustavus Adolphus College, Hofstra University, Ithaca College, Lawrence Technological University, Messiah University, Metropolitan State University, Michigan Technological University, Milwaukee School of Engineering, Northern Arizona University, Pace University, Pepperdine University, Point Park University, Princeton University, Rollins College, Saint Louis University, Stanford University, Stevenson University, Stony Brook University, Suffolk University, SUNY at Albany, The University of Chicago, The University of Michigan, University of Delaware, University of Idaho, University of Indianapolis, University of Miami, University of Rochester, University of Wisconsin Oshkosh, Villanova University, Wake Forest University, Western Michigan University 133 18 Comments Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services 1,682 followers 5d Report this post Looking for a part-time job?\n\nConnect with local businesses looking for part-time workers at the Local Jobs Expo on Friday, September 4th, from 11am-2pm on campus to learn more about local work opportunities! #michigantech #mtu #houghton #careerservices #studentsuccess #mtuhuskies #hancock #houghton #jobsearch #michiganjobs Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services 1,682 followers 6d Report this post While we are ready for the bulk of the fall recruiting season on campus, the only thing missing is YOU! We've got room for more employers to join us during various Career Fests throughout the month of September. \n\nWant to get in on the action and connect with students prior to the Fall Career Fair? \n\nRegister on Handshake: https://bit.ly/4zHSsXP Or email careerfair@mtu.edu for more information and availability! #mtu #huskiesgethired #michigantech #careerservices #jobopportunities 24 2 Comments Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Lexi Cescolini 1w Edited Report this post M. J. Electric, LLC is looking to add a Marketing Coordinator to join our team! Come work with me on all things branding, marketing, social media, events, and graphic design - and bring your creativity to a growing team⚡ \n\nWe’re looking for a driven, creative individual who…\n✅ Knows their way around social media\n✅ Has a creative eye for graphic design\n✅ Has experience with promotional products & merchandise\n✅ Can create engaging content & communications\n✅ Enjoys coordinating events and capturing moments behind the camera\n✅ Is organized and can manage multiple projects\n✅ Brings creativity, initiative & a can-do attitude\n\nNo two days look quite the same in this role. You’ll get to work with social media, graphic design, events, photography, promotional products, communications, branding, and more. If you’re someone who likes to stay busy, enjoys a little variety, and loves turning creative ideas into something real - you'll fit right in!\n\nApply here ➡️ https://lnkd.in/gkRHH8Yg 30 Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Keeley Bernard 2w Report this post 🚀 (IMMEDIATE DEADLINE) Students: Want to Work at NASA? Start Here!\n\nInterested in becoming a NASA intern? NASA is hosting a virtual internship information session where students can connect directly with representatives from Pathways, Early Careers, and OSTEM to learn about opportunities at NASA.\n\n📅 Date: Thursday, August 27, 2026\n⏰ Time: 3:30 PM ET / 2:30 PM CT\n💻 Virtual\n\nDuring the session, you'll learn about:\n🔭 NASA internship opportunities\n📝 How to prepare a strong application\n📄 Resume tips\n🎤 Interview best practices\n💻 Online application assessments\n🌎 Pathways and OSTEM programs\n\n👀 NASA Internship Programs:\n🛰️ OSTEM Internships\n→ Paid, short-term, hands-on internships\n→ Undergraduate through graduate-level students can apply\n→ STEM and non-STEM majors are eligible\n→ Minimum 3.0 GPA\n→ Spring 2027 deadline: September 14, 2026\n\n🚀 Pathways Internships\n→ Longer-term developmental opportunities\n→ Can provide a pathway into federal employment\n→ Minimum 2.9 GPA\n→ Students must meet specific enrollment and degree requirements\n🇺🇸 Important: Applicants must be U.S. citizens to participate in NASA's Pathways, Early Careers, and OSTEM internship programs.\n\n📅 Virtual Event Registration Deadline: August 26, 2026\n🔗 Register for the information session: https://lnkd.in/gcuWpCi4 🔗 Explore NASA internships: https://lnkd.in/gfe6WXn4 Know a student who dreams of working at NASA? Tag them or share this opportunity!\n\n📋 HBCU students: Help me make HBCU Opportunities even more useful by completing my short survey. Your feedback helps me find and share scholarships, internships, fellowships, and other opportunities that align with what students actually need. https://lnkd.in/ghuJDA82 #NASA #NASAInternship #STEM #Internship #CollegeStudents #Engineering #Science #Technology #CareerDevelopment #HBCUOpportunities 663 13 Comments Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Better In Our Back Yard 23,773 followers 1mo Edited Report this post The U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) , led by Secretary Chris Wright , is expected to host a workforce development roundtable tomorrow with mining schools and industry leaders.\n\nThe conversation couldn't come at a better time.\n\nAmerica's ability to build new mines, processing facilities, refineries, and manufacturing plants ultimately depends on one thing: people. \n\nWe need more mining engineers, geologists, metallurgists, environmental scientists, and skilled professionals to support the next generation of critical minerals projects.\n\nNumbers from 2023 tell the story:\n\n🇺🇸 United States\n• 14 accredited mining engineering programs\n• 590 undergraduate mining engineering students\n\n🇨🇳 China\n• 45 mining engineering programs\n• Nearly 12,000 mining engineering students\n\nThe following 14 schools are already doing an incredible job preparing America's future mining workforce: University of Arizona South Dakota Mines Michigan Technological University Montana Technological University Penn State University University of Kentucky Virginia Tech University of Utah West Virginia University University of Nevada, Reno Colorado School of Mines Missouri University of Science and Technology University of Alaska Fairbanks New Mexico Tech\n\nThe challenge extends beyond student enrollment. \n\nExisting programs need greater capacity, additional faculty, modern laboratories, and stronger partnerships with industry. We also need to inspire more high school students to pursue careers in mining, geology, metallurgy, and critical minerals from both the public and private sectors.\n\nCreating a new mining engineering program is a major investment, with costs reaching up to $100 million. That makes it even more important to strengthen the programs we already have while encouraging additional universities to establish mining and mineral processing programs.\n\nAmerica doesn't need another conversation about the workforce. America needs action.\n\nWe hope Friday's roundtable results in meaningful investments that expand existing mining schools, support faculty, attract more students, and create new mining programs. Building a secure domestic critical minerals supply chain starts in the classroom.\n\nAmerica cannot build the mines of tomorrow without educating the workforce of today. 2,065 151 Comments Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Cody Kangas 1mo Report this post At a moment when so much of the national conversation around early-career hiring is framed by uncertainty, Michigan Technological University 's Fall 2026 Career Fair registration data is telling a different story.\n\nWith the calendar now in August, more than 310 employers have already registered—a 4% increase YoY. As of today, only 9% of our available space remains (fewer than 40 booths) for our September 29 fair.\n\nThe real story, however, is the breadth of demand. Manufacturing, civil engineering, construction management, energy, health technology, defense, and many other industries will be represented. Employers are seeking students from nearly every corner of campus—from mechanical, civil and environmental, aerospace, and robotics engineering to data science, cybersecurity, mechatronics, human factors, MIS, finance, nursing, and beyond.\n\nThough disruption and hiring headwinds may exist, these indicators continue to signal strong demand for the industry-ready talent developed at Michigan Tech. For employers still looking at their fall recruiting strategy, we encourage you to register soon! Michigan Tech Career Services 76 Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Heather Holm 1mo Report this post Calling all #engineering students! This is a great, extended internship opportunity with hands-on impact in research & development. #MagnaNextGen Rajeev Verma, Ph.D. Data & Analytics Leader | Controls expert | Educator 1mo Magna’s R&D team in Troy, MI, is seeking an elite Computer Vision Engineering co-op (1 year position) to engineer the future of mobility starting Sept 2026. We are tackling complex, real-world automotive challenges and require top-tier, academically exceptional problem-solvers. If you have deep expertise in CV/Deeplearning, Python, and a relentless drive to turn theoretical concepts into functional, cutting-edge algorithms, we want you. If you have a proven track record of outperforming expectations and are ready to prove your skills on a global stage, step up to the challenge and apply directly below.\nYou must apply through the link below to be considered. If you have demonstrable work products/demos - feel free to DM me. https://lnkd.in/gSWTnfAe R&D- Computer Vision Engineering Intern wd3.myworkdaysite.com 21 Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services 1,682 followers 2mo Report this post There is still time to register as an employer for the Fall Career Fair at Michigan Technological University ! Register on Handshake today to lock in your booth! https://lnkd.in/gjC8b9kJ #michigantech #careerfair #houghtonmi #careerservices …more Register for the Michigan Tech Fall Career Fair Today! 90 Like Comment Share Michigan Tech Career Services reposted this Cody Kangas 3mo Report this post Big week ahead. Looking forward to joining Handshake ’s Jerry Lee and Randy Tarnowski , and Verizon ’s Liz Langemak, PhD for an important conversation at NACE26 in Denver.\n\nThe Class of 2026 is not simply entering the workforce. They’re entering the AI economy. And in many ways, they’re already there.\n\nStudents are using AI to research, brainstorm, write resumes, prepare for interviews, message recruiters, and launch real projects. Employers are beginning to signal what they need. Higher education is working to close the gap. This where career and early talent development has to evolve.\n\nCareer Services can’t just be the place students go at the end of college to find a job. We have to foster an ecosystem that helps connect academic learning, employer expectations, experiential education, and the emerging tools shaping the future of work. And that’s exactly what we’re doing at Michigan Technological University . #NACE2026 National Association of Colleges and Employers 97 4 Comments Like Comment Share Join now to see what you are missing Find people you know at Michigan Tech Career Services Browse recommended jobs for you View all updates, news, and articles Join now Affiliated pages MTU Cooperative Education Program Higher Education Similar pages Michigan Tech College of Engineering Higher Education Houghton, Michigan Michigan Tech College of Computing Higher Education Houghton, MI Michigan Tech International Programs and Services Higher Education Houghton, Michigan Michigan Tech Global Campus Higher Education Houghton, Michigan Michigan Tech College of Sciences and Arts Higher Education Houghton, Michigan Women in Mathematics Think Tanks Stockholm, Stockholm Enterprise Program - Michigan Technological University Higher Education Houghton, Michigan Michigan Technological University Higher Education Houghton, MI Schweitzer Engineering Laboratories (SEL) Utilities Pullman, WA Michigan Tech Great Lakes Research Center Research Services Houghton, MI Show more similar pages Show fewer similar pages Browse jobs Summer Intern jobs 23,466 open jobs Design Engineer jobs 129,783 open jobs Mechanical Engineer jobs 46,392 open jobs Intern jobs 71,196 open jobs Engineer jobs 555,845 open jobs Machine Learning Engineer jobs 148,937 open jobs Scientist jobs 48,969 open jobs Analyst jobs 694,057 open jobs Director of Engineering jobs 19,030 open jobs Environmental Coordinator jobs 11,528 open jobs Apprentice Electrician jobs 2,472 open jobs Electrical Engineering Intern jobs 17,303 open jobs Bioinformatician jobs 18,406 open jobs Web Development Intern jobs 5,464 open jobs MBA Intern jobs 330 open jobs Research Intern jobs 21,678 open jobs Research Assistant jobs 43,677 open jobs Student jobs 634,404 open jobs Digital Marketing Specialist jobs 33,650 open jobs Show more jobs like this Show fewer jobs like this More searches More searches Software Engineer jobs LinkedIn © 2026 About Accessibility User Agreement Privacy Policy Your California Privacy Choices Cookie Policy Copyright Policy Brand Policy Guest Controls Community Guidelines العربية (Arabic) বাংলা (Bangla) Čeština (Czech) Dansk (Danish) Deutsch (German) Ελληνικά (Greek) English (English) Español (Spanish) فارسی (Persian) Suomi (Finnish) Français (French) हिंदी (Hindi) Magyar (Hungarian) Bahasa Indonesia (Indonesian) Italiano (Italian) עברית (Hebrew) 日本語 (Japanese) 한국어 (Korean) मराठी (Marathi) Bahasa Malaysia (Malay) Nederlands (Dutch) Norsk (Norwegian) ਪੰਜਾਬੀ (Punjabi) Polski (Polish) Português (Portuguese) Română (Romanian) Русский (Russian) Svenska (Swedish) తెలుగు (Telugu) ภาษาไทย (Thai) Tagalog (Tagalog) Türkçe (Turkish) Українська (Ukrainian) Tiếng Vi